	R-L   MONITOR   HISTORICAL   SOFTWARE   UPDATE
		
		
								OCT.  1972




1.0	INTRODUCTION
	
	
	1.00	ANCIENT HISTORY	B. L. [BEFORE LARY] AT BROOKLYN POLY


			IN THE BEGINNING THERE WAS A PDP-8,A TELETYPE, AND A TC01/TU55 DECTAPE AND CONTROL UNIT...
		AND RICHARD LARY.("MY GOOD FRIEND",MARIO DENOBILI,1968) ALSO PRESENT WAS PAL III FOR PAPER TAPE INPUT
		AND PAPER TAPE OUTPUT WHICH WAS SELDOM USED AS IT TOOK TOO LONG TO LOAD INTO THE MACHINE FROM THE TTY:
		IT WAS EASIER TO ASSEMBLE BY HAND.SO RICHARD LARY WITH HAS GREAT PROGRAMMING SKILL AND FORTHRIGHT FINGERS
		TOGGLED INTO CORE THE ORIGINAL KEYBOARD MONITOR SYSTEM WHICH
		WHILE IT HAD BUGS,WAS STILL QUITE USEFUL FOR WRITING SUCH PROGRAMS AS:
		POLY BASIC,POLY SNOBOL,POLY LISP,STRING LANGUAGE EIGHT,ETC., AND ALSO FULFILLED THE NEEDS OF THE
		THEN QUITE SMALL PDP-8 PROGRAMMING COMMUNITY NOW KNOWN BY THEIR MEMBERSHIP IN SUCH VARIED ORGANIZATIONS AS:
		W.C.F.M.P.G.,P?S [I?S],FRIENDS OF THE BOSTON MASSACRE,PDP-12 SYSTEMS PROGRAMMING GROUP (DECEASED),ETC.
		THESE BUGS WERE MORE OR LESS PREDICTABLE AND PEOPLE PUT UP WITH THEM FOR A WHILE (3.5 YEARS)


			THE SYSTEM,AS IT WAS WRITTEN THEN,MORE OR LESS FULFILLED THE MAIN REQUIREMENTS
		OF THE TYPICAL ASSEMBLY LANGUAGE PROGRAMMER:
		1)	EDITING OF A FILE FOR CHANGES TO THE SOURCE IN A CONVENIENT MANNER
		 (INSERTION AND DELETION OF TEXT,ETC.)
		2)	QUICKLY ASSEMBLING THE CORRECTED SOURCE PROGRAM
		3)	QUICKLY LOADING THE BINARY PROGRAM INTO CORE AND EXECUTING IT
		4)	EASILY RETURNING TO THE MONITOR WHEN THE PROGRAM DIDN'T WORK BECAUSE OF
		 LOGIC ERRORS IN THE PROGRAM OR SUCESSFUL TERMINATION
		 (BY MURPHY'S LAW THIS CAN NEVER HAPPEN)
		 OF THE PROGRAM AS WRITTEN (NON-BIC PROGRAMS)
		5)	EASY RESTART OF THE MONITOR BY MANUAL MEANS WHICH INCLUDES THE POSSIBILITY OF
		 HAVING TO KEY IN A FEW INSTRUCTIONS TO REPLACE A WIPED OUT BOOTSTRAP IF THE
		 PROGRAM LAST LOADED REALLY BOMBED


			THE MONITOR WAS THUS A REALISTIC SYSTEM BECAUSE IT:
		1)	WAS DESIGNED TO RUN OFF A DECTAPE,THE ONLY MASS STORAGE DEVICE AVAILABLE,
		 A FUNDAMENTALLY SERIAL DEVICE WHICH CAN TAKE MANY TIMES LONGER TO TRANSFER INFORMATION
		 THAN OTHER MASS STORAGE DEVICES (DISKS,DRUMS) UNLESS THIS SERIAL FACTOR IS
		 TAKEN UNDER CONSIDERATION
		 [AS A COROLLARY CONSIDERATION,THE MONITOR'S TAPE ROUTINES CAN READ SEVERAL BLOCKS OF INFORMATION
		 WHICH ARE SEQUENTIAL ON THE TAPE IN ONE SUBROUTINE CALL OPERATION
		 TO ATTEMPT TO READ SEQUENTIAL BLOCKS SEPARATELY WOULD REQUIRE THE TAPE TO BE 
		 TURNED AROUND EACH TIME BECAUSE OF SEARCHING CONSIDERATIONS. THE SYSTEM  WAS DESIGNED TO
		 GENERALLY READ IN SEQUENCES OF TAPE BLOCKS INSTEAD OF WIDELY SCATTERED INDIVIDUAL BLOCKS.
		 THE INABILITY TO READ IN MORE THAN ONE BLOCK AT A TIME AND THE SCATTERING OF BLOCKS DURING
		 SYSTEMS OPERATIONS IS WHAT LED TO THE DOWNFALL OF WHAT IS KNOWN AS:
		 "THE DISK MONITOR SYSTEM ON DECTAPE" (RECENTLY RETIRED) WHICH WAS AND STILL IS THE ONLY
		 PROGRAMMING SYSTEM FOR DEVELOPEMENT ON A 4K MACHINE (YES,GEORGE,THERE ARE 4K MACHINES OUT 
		 THERE IN THE REAL WORLD!!)
		 THERE IS OF COURSE ANOTHER SYSTEM AVAILABLE FROM DEC FOR 4K KNOWN AS THE
		 DECTAPE LIBRARY SYSTEM,WHICH ONLY SAVES CORE IMAGES,WHICH IT DOES VERY NICELY.
		 THIS SYSTEM HAS ACCEPTABLE MULTI-BLOCK I/O AND USES THE STANDARD TC01 BOOTSTRAP
		 IN FACT,IN TERMS OF DESIRABLE SYSTEM FUNCTIONS,THE USE OF THE DECTAPE LIBRARY SYSTEM AND
		 THE R-L MONITOR IN CONJUNCTION WITH EACH OTHER REPRESENTS A VERY DESIRABLE COMBINATION AS
		 THE DECTAPE LIBRARY SYSTEM SAVES CORE IMAGES AND NOTHING ELSE,AND THE
		 R-L MONITOR SYSTEM DOES EVERYTHING ELSE (SEVERAL R-L SUBSYSTEMS WERE CREATED BY TRANSFERRING
		 CORE IMAGES BETWEEN THE TWO SYSTEMS)]
		2)	INCLUDED MANY TAPE MOTION SAVING DEVICES (USE OF A SCRATCH FILE LOCATED NEAR THE
		 BEGINNING OF THE TAPE TO SPEED ASSEMBLIES,A TAPE REWIND COMMAND CHARACTER,^R
		 TO BE USED AT ANY TIME TO SPEED SYSTEM RESPONSE TO COMMAND STRINGS (EX:RUN PAL,^RFILE1,FILE2))
		3)	PUT AS MUCH OF THE SYSTEM AS WAS PRACTICAL INTO CORE AT THE SAME TIME TO ELIMINATE
		 TAPE MOTION ALTOGETHER DURING ANY REASONABLE MONITOR COMMAND (NO SWAPPING UNLESS
		 THE TAPE WAS REQUIRED TO MOVE ANYWAY)
		4)	HAD COMMANDS DESIGNED TO BE EASY TO LEARN FOR THE INEXPERIENCED PROGRAMMER WHICH WERE
		 VERY STRAIGHT-FORWARD (LOAD FILE,SAVE FILE,ETC.) BUT WERE SOPHISTICATED ENOUGH TO
		 SATISFY THE NEEDS OF EVEN THE MOST JADED (GREEN,NOT NECESSARILY J.C.) SYSTEMS PROGRAMMER
		 WITHOUT INSULTING HIM
		5)	HAD A FILE STRUCTURE WHICH WAS NOT ASSEMBLY ORIENTED TO ALLOW THE USE OF HIGH LEVEL LANGUAGES
		 (FOCAL,BASIC,SNOBOL,ETC.) TO HAVE A SYSTEM REASONABLE TO THEIR NEEDS
		 IN OTHER WORDS,CLOSE TO TIME-SHARING AS OFFERED TO USERS OF BASIC,ETC.
		6)	IN CONNECTION WITH 5) ABOVE THE SYSTEM USED LINE NUMBERS TO FULL ADVANTAGE INSTEAD OF THE
		 STANDARD DEC EDITOR SYSTEM WITHOUT LINE NUMBERS CONSIDERED BY MANY TO BE (PUTTING IT MILDLY)
		 LESS THAN IDEAL
		(EDITING NOTE:I JUST HAD TO RETYPE THIS LINE BECAUSE I COULDN'T FIND IT !!)
		 THE FILES WERE STRUCTURED INTERNALLY TO APPEAR TO EITHER HAVE LINE NUMBERS OR NOT
		 DEPENDING ON HOW YOU ACCESSED THE FILE.IN ADDITION THE USE OF LINE NUMBERS
		 PROVIDED A PERMANENT RECORD OF THE SOURCE AS THE LATEST STRING INSERTED CAN BE VERIFIED
		 FROM THE TELETYPE LISTING WHERE IT WAS TYPED.THIS SAVED MUCH TIME OVER REPEATED LISTING
		 OF THE SOURCE FILE AS IS REQUIRED WITH OTHER EDITING SYSTEMS
		 IN ADDITION THE USE OF THE LINE NUMBERS DIDN'T MATERIALLY SLOW DOWN THE LISTING OF THE FILE,
		 IN FACT IT MADE IT EASIER TO VERIFY WHICH SECTION OF A LISTING WAS DESIRED TO BE REPEATED
		 (OF NO CONSEQUENCE FOR A COMPLETE LISTING)
		 ALSO THE SYSTEM PROVIDED TEXT ORIENTED COMMANDS TO BE COMPATIBLE WITH THE
		 NON-LINE NUMBER SYSTEMS AND THE BASIC PAPER-TAPE SYSTEM 
		 (THE PUNCH COMMAND PUTS OUT LEADER-TRAILER OF USER CONTROLLED LENGTH ALONG WITH
		 THE PRECISE TEXT DESIRED ALL WITHOUT LINE NUMBERS WHICH ARE MEANINGLESS TO
		 PAPER TAPE PROGRAMS WHICH RECEIVE INFORMATION SOLELY FORM THE PAPER TAPE READER)
		7)	HAD A BATCH FACILITY READ IN FROM A PREVIOUSLY PREPARED COMMAND FILE (ADAPTABLE TO CARDS,
		 PAPER TAPE,ETC) TO ALLOW THE SYSTEM TO RUN ITSELF FOR SEVERAL HOURS IN TYPICAL
		 LONG TERM USAGE.THE TYPICAL PROGRAMMER'S ENVIRONMENT ALLOWS HIM TO LEAVE HIS WORK FOR SEVERAL HOURS
		 AT A TIME (TO GO OUT TO EAT,GO HOME,GO TO SLEEP ETC.)
		 THUS LACKING A LINE PRINTER,THE PROGRAMMER NOW HAD A PAINLESS WAY OF LISTING HIS PROGRAMS FOR
		 FURTHER USE WITHOUT ACTUALLY WAITING AROUND TO DIRECT THE SYSTEM EVERY FEW MINUTES
		 (HOW MANY PROGRAMMER'S IN THE REAL WORLD (OUTSIDE MAYNARD) WOULD LIKE A LISTING
		 OF THEIR PROGRAM BUT DECIDED AGAINST IT DUE TO TIME CONSIDERATION,SHARED MACHINE TIME,ETC.
		 AT BROOKLYN POLY,THIS SITUATION PREVAILS DUE TO THE NUMBER OF PEOPLE WAITING TO USE THE MACHINE.
		 BUT A LINE PRINTER IS CONSIDERED A LUXURY AT THIS INSTALLATION.
		 ASK THE PEOPLE WHO HAVE MULTI-COLORED LISTINGS FROM A TELETYPE FOR FURTHER INFORMATION:
		 (RED = TUESDAY' CORRECTIONS TO MONDAY'S YELLOW CHANGES TO LAST FRIDAY'S GREEN EDITING NOTES,ETC.)
		 (THERE ARE AVAILABLE UP TO 50 DISTINCT COLORS OF COLORED PENCILS FROM AT LEAST 2 DIFFERENT
		 MANUFACTURERS FOR THOSE WHO ARE HARD PRESSED))
		 IN SHORT,THE SYSTEM FULFILLED THE NEED OF MANY PEOPLE FOR SEVERAL YEARS WITH EMPHASIS ON
		 EASE OF PROGRAMMING. (LACK OF SYSTEM INTERFERENCE WITH PROGRAMMING THOUGHT AND EFFORT.)
		 (LET'S SEE,WAS THAT LINE  SIX LINES AGO,OR WAS IT 7 ?,I DON'T REMEMBER,I'LL HAVE TO LIST IT TO MAKE SURE !)
		 AND RECOGNITION OF THE EDITING AND DEBUGGING PHASES OF THE PROGRAM
		 (ONCE A PROGRAM WORKS IT DOESN'T MUCH MATTER WHICH SYSTEM RUNS IT,AS LONG AS IT TAKES
		 UNDER AN HOUR TO LOAD THE BINARY. ("PAPER TAPE IS BAD FOR YOU!"
						JOHN C. GREEN 1971))
	2.00	MODERN HISTORY	A. M.	(AFTER MOUTH)


			IN 1970 THE P?S SENT OUT A SMALL BUT MIGHTY BAND OF HACKERS
		TO FIGHT THE BUGS INHERENT IN THE R-L MONITOR. DURING THE FIERCE BATTLES THAT ENSUED
		FOR THE NEXT 1.5 YEARS THE P?S LOST A FEW MEMBERS TO OUTSIDE FORCES
		(MARRIAGE,THE DRAFT,DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION,SCIENCE FICTION WRITING,
		OTHER SCHOOLS,WORKING,BEACHCOMBING,GENERAL BUMMING AROUND,IBM,BUBONIC PLAGO,ETC)
		BUT A FEW PERSISTED AND WERE ABLE TO OVERCOME THE PROBLEMS
		IN THE INTERIM SEVERAL IMPORTANT RESULTS WERE ACHIEVED:
		1)	THE SYSTEM WAS MADE TO WORK ON A DF32 DISK WHICH FORESAW THE FEASIBILITY
		 OF USING OTHER DEVICES FOR THE SYSTEM DEVICE SUCH AS PDP-12 LINCTAPE,RF08 DISK,RK08 DISK PACK,
		 MAGNETIC TAPE, AND THE AS OF THEN UNHEARD OF TD8/E SIMPLE DECTAPE
		2)	SEVERAL SUBSYSTEMS WERE MADE TO RUN WITHOUT EAE
		3)	SEVERAL SUBSYSTEMS WERE ADDED TO THE SYSTEM (EX: FOCAL)
		4)	MULTI-UNIT SUPPORT FOR THE SYSTEM WAS ADDED (SYS N)
		5)	IMPROVEMENTS TO PAL III WERE MADE SUCH AS BINARY OUTPUT FILES
		6)	REVOLUTIONARY TAPE ROUTINES WERE WRITTEN:
			A)	FOR THE BINARY LOADER A SMALLER TAPE SEARCH ALGORITHM WAS DISCOVERED
			 WHICH RELIED ON TWO FACTORS WHICH ARE PECULIAR TO THE BINARY LOADER
			 (NOT GENERAL PURPOSE) NAMELY:
				I)	LACK OF NEED TO SEARCH FOR BLOCK ZERO AND THUS INCUR AN END ERROR
				II)	THE FACT THAT STANDARD FORMAT  TAPES HAVE BLOCK NUMBERS 11 OR LESS BITS
				  IN LENGTH (SIGNIFICANTLY) LEAVING THE SIGN BIT OF THE AC
				  AVAILABLE FOR OTHER TESTS
			 THIS ALLOWED THE BINARY LOADER TO USE THE STANDARD TC01 BOOTSTRAP
			 FOR SAFETY AND COMPATIBILITY AND LIFTED THE 5 BINARY FILE RESTRICTION TO
			 15 (GENERALLY OTHER SUB-SYSTEMS SUCH AS PAL ALLOW 17)
			 ALSO A SUPPORT FOR EXTENDED MEMORY BECAME POSSIBLE ALTHOUGH IT COULD NOT BE IMPLEMENTED
			 IN PAL III (PAL IS TIGHT;IT IS NEARLY IMPOSSIBLE TO MODIFY AS ISSUED;
			 BEAR IN MIND THAT THE R-L SUB-SYSTEM KNOWN AS PAL IS AN OVERLAY TO DEC'S PAPER TAPE !)
			 AS THE FIELD PSEUDO-OP COULD NOT BE MODIFIED AND WAS CONSIDERED
			 WORTHLESS IN-HOUSE FOR A 4-K MACHINE ANYWAY.THIS WAS BEFORE THE P?S ASSEMBLER.
			B)	THE DECTAPE ROUTINES WRITTEN FOR 1 PAGE WHICH HAVE BEEN CIRCULATED
				THROUGHOUT PDP-8 LAND WERE SUPPLANTED WITH A MUCH MORE EFFICIENT
			 VERSION WHICH WAS THEN SUPPLANTED WITH A MORE EFFICIENT VERSION WHICH WAS OPTIMIZED
			 BY RICHARD LARY THUS ENSURING ITS RELIABILITY AS A TAPE ROUTINE
			 THIS TAPE ROUTINE WAS MODIFIED FOR 7600-7753 OPERATION (FIELD 0)
			 INCLUDING THE STANDARD TC01 BOOTSTRAP AND SYSTEM LOADER AS IT IS KNOWN 
			 (THE SYSTEM LOADER IS AN INTERNAL CALL TO THE SYSTEM I/O ROUTINES TO
			 LOAD SUB-SYSTEMS (CORE IMAGES) SUCH AS PAL,BIN,EDIT,SNOBOL,FOCAL,ETC)
			 THERE WAS EVEN ROOM FOR ERROR RECOVERY,MULTI-FIELD AND MULTI-UNIT SUPPORT
			 THIS EFFECTIVELY ALLOWED THE SYSTEM TO HAVE ONE EXTRA PAGE FOR OTHER PURPOSES
			 (SUCH AS SUPPORT OF TD8/E TAPE ROUTINES,ETC.)
			 THE TC01/TC08 VERSION THUS ALLOWED THE USER TO CALL THE TAPE ROUTINES
			 INTO CORE FOR HIS OWN USE JUST BY ROCKING THE TAPE OFF THE END ZONE
			 SIMILAR TO THE TC01 BOOTSTRAP.THIS SAVES TIME BY ELIMINATING THE SOURCE
			 OF A DECTAPE ROUTINE I THE USER'S PROGRAM
			 A UNIQUE FEATURE OF THESE TAPE ROUTINES IS THE CORRECT CALCULATION OF
			 INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION BY REMEMBERING THE PREVIOUS BLOCK NUMBER REFERENCED
			 AS OF OCTOBER 1972 THESE ROUTINES HAVE BEEN OPTIMIZED 14 MORE TIMES AND NOW INCLUDE STANDARDIZED
			 ENTRY POINTS AND PARAMETER LOCATIONS FOR FIELD UNIT,SYSTEM LOADER,ETC
			 UNIFIED BUFFERING CAPABILITY COMPATIBLE WITH THE OTHER
			 KNOWN SYSTEM HANDLERS,(LINCTAPE,DF32 ETC.) MEANING A STANDARD WAIT LOOP
			 IN THE SAME PLACE AS THE OTHERS' AND USE OFT THE TC01 BOOTSTRAP AS THE
			 WAIT SUBROUTINE AS ORIGINALLY INTENDED THUS ALLOWING A SINGLE WAIT LOOP
			 FOR ALL PURPOSES (IMPROVING BUFFERING)
		7)	A NEW ASSEMBLER WAS STARTED TO REPLACE PAL III AND ALL OTHERS EVENTUALLY
		8)	THE DUP COMMAND WAS REWRITTEN TO ALLOW FOR MULTIPLE TAPE DRIVE SUPPORT
		 AND TO MAKE USE OF THE NEW TAPE ROUTINES AND RESIDENT BOOTSTRAP
		9)	THE BIN COMMAND WAS REWRITTEN TO HAVE COMPATIBILITY WITH ALL LOADERS
		 THE TC01 BOOTSTRAP,RIM LOADER AND BIN LOADER WERE NOW ALL IN 7600 AT THE SAME TIME
		 WITH FULL COMPATIBILITY WITH THE STANDARD DEC BINARY LOADER INCLUDING SOME PREVIOUSLY
		 IGNORED OR LIMITED FEATURES INCLUDING SWITCH REGISTER REQUEST FOR HI-SPEED READER AND EXTENDED MEMORY
		 THE PREVIOUS LOADER BOMBED ON FIELD SETTINGS PUNCHED IN THE INPUT TAPES,EVEN TO FIELD 0 !
		 THAT BUG LED TO INVALID LOADING AND A CHECKSUM ERROR 
		 DUE TO A BUG NOW CORRECTED
		 10)	SEVERAL TAPE BOOTSTRAPS WERE WRITTEN INCLUDING 1 THREE INSTRUCTIONS LONG WHICH IS
		  UNIVERSAL TO MOST SYSTEMS REWUIRING  RELOCATION FOR SOME SYSTEMS IF NECESSARY
		 BUT COULD BE RELOCATED FOR ALL SYSTEMS ANYWAY (RELOCATION GENERALLY REQUIRES MORE SWITCH
		 MANIPULATION TO BOOTSTRAP)
		11)	A SPECIAL BOOTSTRAP WAS WRITTEN WHICH GAVE THE USER THE MOST SEQUENTIAL
		  CORE AVAILABLE (0-7755),WHILE STILL MAINTAINING A BOOTSTRAP WHICH
		 EXACTLY OVERLAYS THE STANDARD DEC RIM LOADER
		12)	WORK WAS STARTED ON A TOTALLY REVISED VERSION OF THE MONITOR WHICH
		  INTERNALLY CODED DIFFERENTLY BUT EXTERNALLY REMAINED THE SAME,TO ALLOW SEVERAL NEW FEATURES TO BE ADDED
		12)	THE NEW ASSEMBLER MENTIONED ABOVE IN 7) WAS NEARLY COMPLETED AND THEN 
		  MODIFIED TO BE COMPATIBLE WITH THE THE MONITOR AND THEN MODIFIED TO ADD MANY HERETOFORE UNAVAILABLE
		  FEATURES TO A 4-K ASSEMBLER (SOME ARE COMPLETELY ORIGINAL) SUCH AS OUTPUT BUFFERING
		  FOR INCREASED SPEED (I AM SMALL AND I AM FAST !,WATCH ME ASSEMBLE PDP-8 PROGRAMS !!)
